        <section id="section-1" class="legal-section">
          <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
          <p>
            When you interact with Flixes, we collect information necessary to provide and secure our virtual card services, facilitate user authentication, and ensure platform safety. We collect information in two main categories:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Information you provide directly:</strong> When signing in with Google, you authorize Google to share certain profile information with us.</li>
            <li><strong>Technical and usage information automatically collected:</strong> Information automatically gathered by our servers when you browse or interact with our portal, including IP address, browser type, device information, operating system, and access timestamps.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="section-2" class="legal-section">
          <h2>2. Google OAuth 2.0 User Data Collection & Usage</h2>
          <p>
            Flixes uses Google OAuth 2.0 Single Sign-On to verify your identity and allow you to log into our platform seamlessly and securely. When you choose to authenticate using Google, we request the following Google OAuth scopes:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><code>openid</code>: A unique, persistent Google account identifier (Google Subject ID) used to match your session with your Flixes account.</li>
            <li><code>email</code>: Your primary Google email address, used to identify your account, communicate critical transactional updates, and verify admin/user privileges.</li>
            <li><code>profile</code>: Your basic public profile information, including your full name, display name, and profile picture/avatar URL, used to personalize your dashboard interface.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            During the OAuth authentication process, Google also issues temporary OAuth 2.0 access tokens and, where authorized, refresh tokens. These tokens are stored securely in encrypted server-side sessions strictly to maintain your authenticated login state without requiring you to re-authenticate on every page visit.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="section-3" class="legal-section highlight-box">
          <h2>3. Google API Services User Data Policy Compliance (Limited Use)</h2>
          <p class="limited-use-statement">
            <strong>Flixes' use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.</strong>
          </p>
          <p>In strict adherence to these Limited Use requirements:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>We only use Google user data to provide and improve user-facing features that are prominent in the Flixes user interface.</li>
            <li>We do <strong>not</strong> transfer Google user data to third parties, except as strictly necessary to provide or improve these user-facing features, comply with applicable laws, or as part of a merger/acquisition with user consent.</li>
            <li>We do <strong>not</strong> use Google user data to serve advertisements, including personalized, re-targeted, or interest-based advertising.</li>
            <li>We do <strong>not</strong> allow humans to read Google user data unless we have obtained your affirmative agreement for specific messages, doing so is necessary for security purposes (such as investigating abuse), to comply with applicable law, or our use is limited to internal operations using aggregated and de-identified data.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="section-4" class="legal-section">
          <h2>4. How We Use Your Information</h2>
          <p>We use the data we collect solely for the following legitimate business purposes:</p>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>Account Creation & Authentication:</strong> Creating, provisioning, and maintaining your personal Flixes user account and verifying your identity upon sign-in.</li>
            <li><strong>Service Delivery:</strong> Providing access to the Flixes portal dashboard, virtual card catalogs, packages, and member-only features.</li>
            <li><strong>Security & Abuse Prevention:</strong> Protecting our platform, systems, and users from fraudulent access, unauthorized account takeovers, brute-force attacks, and malicious bot activity.</li>
            <li><strong>Customer Support & Administrative Notices:</strong> Responding to user inquiries, resolving technical issues, and sending important operational notifications regarding terms, privacy updates, or account status.</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section id="section-5" class="legal-section">
          <h2>5. Sharing and Disclosure of Data</h2>
          <p>
            <strong>We do not sell, rent, trade, or monetize your personal information or Google user data under any circumstances.</strong> We only disclose information in the limited scenarios described below:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Hosting and Infrastructure Providers:</strong> Our application is hosted on Vercel Inc. Infrastructure providers process server logs and traffic strictly to ensure website reliability and availability.</li>
            <li><strong>Internal Security Notifications:</strong> For platform security, automated login notification alerts (containing email, name, IP address, and timestamp) are sent to an internal administrative Discord webhook monitored exclusively by authorized Flixes system administrators to rapidly detect and prevent unauthorized account access.</li>
            <li><strong>Legal Obligations:</strong> We may disclose information if required to do so by law, subpoena, court order, or governmental regulatory authority.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="section-6" class="legal-section">
          <h2>6. Cookies & Session Management</h2>
          <p>
            Flixes uses strictly necessary first-party HTTP cookies via <code>express-session</code>. These cookies store an encrypted session identifier on your device to remember that you are logged in. We do not use third-party tracking cookies or advertising pixels.
          </p>
          <p>
            You can manage or disable cookies via your browser settings; however, disabling cookies will prevent you from signing in and accessing your Flixes account.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="section-7" class="legal-section">
          <h2>7. Data Storage, Security & Retention</h2>
          <p>
            We implement robust, industry-standard administrative, physical, and technical security measures to protect your information:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>All network communications are encrypted in transit using <strong>TLS/HTTPS</strong>.</li>
            <li>Session cookies are configured with <code>httpOnly</code> protection to mitigate Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) risks.</li>
            <li>Access to backend servers and administrative consoles is restricted to authenticated, authorized administrators with multi-factor authentication.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            <strong>Data Retention:</strong> We retain your account data (name, email, join date) for as long as your account remains active or as needed to provide you with the services. If you request account deletion, your personal data will be permanently purged within thirty (30) days.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="section-8" class="legal-section">
          <h2>8. Your Rights & Data Deletion Instructions</h2>
          <p>You have full control over your personal data:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Access & Correction:</strong> You have the right to request a copy of the personal information we hold about you and request corrections if inaccurate.</li>
            <li><strong>Revoking Google Access:</strong> You can disconnect Flixes from your Google account at any time by visiting your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Account Security & Third-Party Permissions</a> page and clicking "Remove Access".</li>
            <li><strong>Account & Data Deletion Request:</strong> If you wish to permanently delete your account, session records, and all associated personal data from Flixes, please send an email to <a href="mailto:zohaibjuttsaab1234@gmail.com">zohaibjuttsaab1234@gmail.com</a> with the subject line <code>"Data Deletion Request"</code> from your registered email address. We will verify your identity and delete all associated records within thirty (30) business days, sending you written confirmation once complete.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="section-9" class="legal-section">
          <h2>9. Children's Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Flixes does not knowingly collect or solicit personal information from individuals under the age of 18 (or the age of legal majority in your jurisdiction). If we learn that we have inadvertently collected personal data from a child under the legal age, we will take immediate steps to delete that information from our servers.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="section-10" class="legal-section">
          <h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
